 "Click a block. Orange blocks are long-term stores that live outside the model (files, a database, a vector index).": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Where each lives</0>": "",
 "The model itself is stateless between calls: <0>all</0> \"memory\" is text that the harness puts back into the context window.": "",
 "Working memory = the current context. Long-term memory = an <0>external store</0> the agent reads and writes through tools or the harness.": "",
 "Long-term stores are often split into semantic (facts), episodic (past events) and procedural (how-to) memory, a loose analogy to human memory.": "",
 "These categories are a design vocabulary, not a standard; products name and implement them differently.": "",
 "Writing to long-term memory is a side effect: decide what gets saved, and treat recalled text as untrusted input (see <0>prompt injection</0>).": "",
