 "▼ Dive in: <0>Hybrid + RRF</0>": "",
 "Vector search finds <0>meaning</0>, keyword search (BM25) finds <1>exact terms</1> (names, error codes, IDs). Hybrid search combines both.": "",
 "Reciprocal rank fusion (RRF) merges ranked lists using only <0>ranks</0>, so scores from different systems need no calibration.": "",
 "A reranker re-scores the top candidates with a heavier model; agentic RAG lets the model call retrieval as a <0>tool</0>, decide when to search, and refine queries.": "",
 "Typical recipe (not a rule): retrieve ~{#} candidates cheaply, rerank to ~{#}, then prompt.": "",
 "RRF constant k = {#} is a common default from the original paper; it is tunable.": "",
 "Agentic RAG can improve hard questions but adds latency, cost and more ways to loop; measure it (see <0>evals</0>).": "",
