 "Example: a doc ranked 1st by BM25 and 3rd by cosine gets {#}/({#}+{#}) + {#}/({#}+{#}) = <0>{#}</0>. Appearing high in <1>both</1> lists wins.": "",
 "Reranking would then take these fused candidates and re-score each (query, chunk) pair with a cross-encoder or an LLM, which reads both texts together and is slower but usually more precise (tends to help; measure on your data).": "",
